From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 05:02:23 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: cubie-a7s: Add the CPU cluster
 supplies

DCDC3 and DCDC5 of the AXP318W supply the Cortex-A76 cores (vdd-cpub)
and the Cortex-A55 cores (vdd-cpul). Describe both from 0.8 V, the
typical voltage of the A733 datasheet (V0.93, section 5.3, Table 5-2,
which lists no minimum or maximum), to 1.05 V, an upper bound that the
datasheet does not give, not measured, and keep them always-on until
cpufreq uses them.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on two boards; DCDC3 and DCDC5
register as vdd-cpub and vdd-cpul, enabled within their limits and with
no consumer, and dmesg shows no regulator warning; cpufreq is not used.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 .../boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts   | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
index 04e2f5614ebb..fb15a32fa5f2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733-cubie-a7s.dts
@@ -208,6 +208,20 @@ reg_swout2: swout2 {
 				regulator-name = "vcc-io";
 				regulator-always-on;
 			};
+
+			reg_dcdc3: dcdc3 {
+				regulator-name = "vdd-cpub";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1050000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
+
+			reg_dcdc5: dcdc5 {
+				regulator-name = "vdd-cpul";
+				regulator-min-microvolt = <800000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1050000>;
+				regulator-always-on;
+			};
 		};
 	};
 };
